# Local profile: one operator, no proxy, reached at 127.0.0.1 only. Never tunnel,
# forward or publish this. Local mode is host-loopback only: it rejects DASHBOARD_ORIGIN,
# CF_ACCESS_* and DASHBOARD_OWNER outright and requires DASHBOARD_BIND=127.0.0.1, so this
# profile runs the app directly on the host and never inside a container — a container must
# bind its own interface, which requires hosted mode with container-private-interface
# (see env.hosted.example).
DASHBOARD_MODE=local
DASHBOARD_EXPOSURE=host-loopback
DASHBOARD_BIND=127.0.0.1
PORT=4319
# A host path owned by the account that runs this profile (the systemd unit's user), not the
# container's /data volume (that belongs to the hosted profile). systemd's EnvironmentFile does
# not expand variables, so give an absolute path under that account's home — for example
# /home/<user>/.local/share/pilot-data — and make sure that directory exists and is writable by it.
DASHBOARD_DATA=/home/<user>/.local/share/pilot-data
# Enable bounded file-edit capability for agents with the file_edit scope (default off).
# DASHBOARD_FILE_EDIT=on
